[Event "Alekhine: Modern"]

{The Alekhine (1...Nf6) invites White's pawns forward and then attacks them.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... Nf6 {[%cal Gf6e4] The Alekhine. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
2. e5 {Gains time. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
2... Nd5 {Central knight.}
3. d4 {Centre.}
3... d6 {Hits e5. The pawn on d6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
4. Nf3 {The Modern.}
4... Bg4 {Pins. The bishop on g4 eyes the knight on f3.}
 (4... g6 {Fianchetto.}
5. Bc4 {Hits the knight. The bishop on c4 eyes the knight on d5.}
5... Nb6 {Retreats. The knight on b6 eyes the bishop on c4 and controls d5.}
6. Bb3 {Retreats. The bishop on b3 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
6... Bg7 {Develops. The bishop on g7 eyes the pawn on e5.}
7. a4 {Gains space.}
)
5. Be2 {Unpins.}
5... e6 {Solid.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... Be7 {Develops.}
7. c4 {Kicks the knight. The pawn on c4 eyes the knight on d5.}
7... Nb6 {Retreats. The knight on b6 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls d5.}
8. h3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on h3 eyes the bishop on g4.}
8... Bh5 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on h5 eyes the knight on f3.}
9. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
9... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
10. Be3 {Develops.}
10... d5 {Fixes the centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.} *

[Event "Alekhine: Four Pawns & 2.Nc3"]

{The Four Pawns Attack is the critical test. 2.Nc3 avoids the theory.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... Nf6 {Alekhine. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
2. e5 {Gains time. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
 (2. Nc3 {Avoids the Alekhine. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
2... e5 {Central reply. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
3... Nc6 {Four Knights. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
)
2... Nd5 {Central.}
3. c4 {Kicks. The pawn on c4 eyes the knight on d5.}
3... Nb6 {Retreats. The knight on b6 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls d5.}
4. d4 {Centre.}
4... d6 {Hits e5. The pawn on d6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
5. f4 {The Four Pawns.}
 (5. exd6 {The Exchange variation. The pawn on d6 eyes the pawn on c7 and the pawn on e7.}
5... cxd6 {Recaptures toward the centre, keeping a solid pawn majority.}
6. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
6... g6 {[%csl Gg7] Fianchetto aiming at d4.}
)
5... dxe5 {Takes. The pawn on e5 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on f4.}
6. fxe5 {Recaptures.}
6... Nc6 {Hits d4. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5 and the pawn on d4.}
7. Be3 {Defends.}
7... Bf5 {Develops. The bishop on f5 eyes the knight on b1 and controls e4.}
8. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
8... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
9. Nf3 {Develops.}
9... Be7 {Develops.} *
